Yes — there is a real, documented house style. Here it is.

## The chain of authority

`~/DEV/Education_Content_Agent/context/house-style.md` (Format 2, "the one-pager") is the governing doc. It names:
- **Brand file:** `~/DEV/TechEd_Prop/ShitfWave/baylor-brand.css`
- **Precedent artifact:** the ShiftWave protocol card in `~/DEV/TechEd_Prop/ShitfWave/`
- **Build path:** HTML → `html-to-pdf` skill. "Never hand-laid-out."

`~/DEV/Education_Content_Agent/commands/onepager.md` confirms the same. **Best single file to copy from: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/TechEd_Prop/ShitfWave/option-c-matrix.html`** (16 KB, self-contained, print-ready).

## Exact hex colors (from option-c-matrix.html, the printed precedent)

| Hex | Role |
|---|---|
| `#1E1F1F` | Sheet ground (charcoal). Print spec calls for **rich black build, not 100% K** |
| `#154734` | Baylor Green — used only as a radial wash: `rgba(21,71,52,.55)` |
| `#FFB81C` | Baylor Gold — **all rules** (2px `border-top`), headline emphasis, key labels, badge fills |
| `#E0DDD1` | Primary body text on dark (bone) |
| `#D2D3D3` | Secondary/mechanism text |
| `#AFD2C0` | Mint — secondary org line, sub-labels |
| `#FFFFFF` | Headlines, primary org lockup |
| `rgba(255,184,28,.4)` | Hairline under column headers |
| `rgba(224,221,209,.14)` | Interior cell dividers |
| `#4E5150` | Screen-only backdrop behind the sheet (not printed) |

Confirmed: Baylor Green is `#154734`, Gold is `#FFB81C` — the assumption holds. Gold is the workhorse accent; green is a wash, not a fill.

## Fonts

`baylor-brand.css` (1.6 MB — fonts and logo marks embedded as data URIs, zero external deps) declares:

```css
